        "summary": "AMD (AMD) CEO Lisa Su has had a remarkable September, with her rise to prominence as one of the most respected CEOs in tech. Su was pictured with her husband, Daniel Lin, at President Trump's table at the state dinner with Chinese President Xi Jinping and sat next to Tesla (TSLA) CEO Elon Musk and SpaceX CEO Elon Mus. The company's market cap crossed the $1 trillion mark for the first time on Monday, and shares are expected to close above that level later this week. AMD's stock is up 193% year to date, surpassing the 22% gain for Nvidia. The chipmaker also unveiled its next-generation AI chips, including the Instinct MI450 Series GPUs and the 6th Gen EPYC Venice CPUs. The new chips are designed to power AMD's new Helios rack-scale AI systems.",
        "shortSummary": "AMD CEO Lisa Su had a stellar September, with record revenue and significant wins, including meeting President Trump and being inducted into the Wall of Titans.",
